ta-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∬</mo><mi>D</mi></munder><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>In our case, the region <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"82\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D437 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and its boundary <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"83\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D436 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-126532-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-126532-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>Since <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"84\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D443 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx